    "text": "Translating long-term memory into embodied plans is a specific architectural sub-problem that arises when solving partial observability and overwritten world states, not a challenge that exists independently of those problems.",
    "topic": "Dependency relationship"
  },
  {
    "text": "WorldLines addresses the translation of long-term memory into embodied plans as one concrete implementation pathway to handle partial observability and memory overwriting.",
    "topic": "WorldLines method scope"
  },
  {
    "text": "Being a sub-problem of partial observability does not preclude translating memory into plans from having its own distinct technical difficulties and solution constraints.",
    "topic": "Non-triviality of sub-problems"
  },
  {
    "text": "The classification of a problem as not 'independent' and the recognition of its practical importance are not mutually exclusive; it can be a significant sub-challenge while still deriving its relevance from a broader problem.",
    "topic": "Independence vs. significance"
  }
